<title>CANADA: Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.911.</title>
<headline>Bank of Canada 91-day T-bill yields avg 2.911.</headline>
<dateline>OTTAWA 1996-11-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Canada said the average yield at this week's auction of C$2.4 billion of 91-day Government of Canada treasury bills due February 13, 1997 was 2.911 percent, down from 2.913 percent last week.</p>
<p>The average yield on C$1.3 billion of 175-day T-bills due May 8, 1997 was 3.081 percent, up from 3.067 percent last week, and on C$1.2 billion of 364-day T-bills due November 13, 1997 was 3.350 percent, down from 3.410 percent.</p>
<p>The Bank bought C$700 million three-month, C$200 million six-month and C$175 million one-year bills. It holds C$1.25 billion of C$5.4 billion of bills due Nov. 21</p>
